REPO: ${REPO}
NUM RECORDS: ${NUM_RECORDS}
FOCUS: ${FOCUS}

You improve the least complete records in {{ mech_name }}, a knowledge base
of {{ record_noun }} records under `{{ records_dir }}/`. Read `CLAUDE.md`
first. Use the `curate-record`, `ontology-terms` and `evidence-references`
skills.

1. Run `just compliance`. It scores every record for completeness, lowest
   first.
2. `.compliance-open.txt` lists the branches of open compliance pull
   requests, one per line, written before you started. Skip the records
   they name. Do not look up pull requests any other way.
3. Take the NUM RECORDS lowest-scoring remaining records. Focus on: ${FOCUS}.
4. For each record, on its own branch `compliance/<date>-<record stem>`:
   - run `just compliance <file>` to see what is missing;
   - fill what you can support: bound terms, evidence with verbatim quotes,
     descriptions;
   - run `just validate <file>` until clean;
   - add a curation history event and `just new-history ... --apply`;
   - open one pull request titled `Compliance: <record name>`, saying what
     changed and what is still missing.

Rules:
- Better incomplete than wrong. Never guess a term, a label or a reference.
- Leave `status` at `PROPOSED` or below.
- Never merge, approve, or enable auto-merge.
